    "recipientRequirementScope": "R3 as frozen was tested on a recipient that page-level DOM can identify. There the fenced extension refused every swap. It does not hold for a recipient inside a closed shadow root: the extension binds the host element, and with a swap inside the component both trusted extension modes delivered to the wrong internal target in 10 of 10 trials and reported success. 'No delivery to a different element' is therefore established for the extension only where the actual recipient can be verified from the page's DOM."
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "A reviewed click covers one top-level document, one compositor surface, device scale 1 and page scale 1; frames with child surfaces, video or overlay-candidate resources end a review.",
    "A repaint after admission does not cancel the click; the recipient is re-checked in the page process at delivery.",
    "Renderer restart, navigation and GPU-process loss end a review; a fresh review works afterwards (lifecycle.json and the invalidation cases).",
    "The browser cannot promise anything about later server writes. Record identity, version checks and duplicate suppression belong to the application.",
    "The workspace's reviewed click and inbox accept only a canvas target today. The browser commands accept any rectangle; a DOM button passes at browser level (dom-button-delivers).",
    "The agent that prepares the change in the inbox test is a scripted stand-in. No model was called and nothing was paid."
  ],
  "notRun": [
    "hardware GPU of any kind",
    "official or PGO build",
    "an outside user or a model-driven agent"
  ]
}
